
WITH DuplicateRecords AS
(
    SELECT *,
           ROW_NUMBER() OVER (
               PARTITION BY name, class, email
               ORDER BY id
           ) AS rn
    FROM Student
)
DELETE FROM DuplicateRecords
WHERE rn > 1;

/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
OVER() → calculates across rows while keeping the original rows.

What is happening?
    PARTITION BY name, class, email

Groups records that are duplicates.
    ORDER BY id

keeps the record with the smallest id as rn = 1.
    WHERE rn > 1